  "note": "\"Polling took place on Thursday for the election of nine urban councillors ... As the elections take place only every three years, the keenest interest was taken in the contest.\" All the old councillors stood again, with two new candidates, John Nugent (auctioneer) and Philip Mone (publican); a third, Thomas Mallon, withdrew (Armagh Guardian). P. J. M'Cann, town clerk, declared the poll shortly after 10 o'clock. Out of a register of 289, 232 polled and two papers were spoiled (the Armagh Guardian gives 287 voters). \"The Council is entirely composed of Nationalists, Mr George M'Bride, J.P., one of the defeated candidates, being the only Unionist on the board for many years\"; the elected are labelled from that sentence, and no label is printed for O'Neill. Arthurs was chairman; Smyth, Watters and M'Bride are styled J.P."
}
